From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Darrel=20Gri=C3=ABt?= <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] v10: Deliver update requests immediately on minnow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shared v10 backend delivers scene-graph update requests from the
hwcomposer vsync callback. With swap() no longer waiting for vsync on
minnow, that phase-locking only adds latency. Measured
requestUpdate->deliver averaged ~15 ms, up to one vsync period, of
input-to-render lag.

Deliver on a zero-interval timer instead. Delivery latency drops to
~0.7 ms with no cadence regression: two-vsync-period frames during
animation stayed at 0-1%. Touch dragging feels responsive as a result.
Updates still queue while the display is blanked, and a static scene
still stops rendering.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow command-mode panel specific]
Signed-off-by: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
---
 hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp | 14 +++++---------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
@@ -338,16 +338,12 @@
     if (m_displayOff && !m_ambientMode)
         return true;
 
-    // Deliver update requests from the vsync callback (see notifyVsync), so
-    // rendering is phase-locked to the display instead of paced by a timer
-    // that drifts against it. The scene graph only asks for another update if
-    // something actually changed, so a static scene still stops rendering.
-    m_updatePending.storeRelease(1);
-
-    // Fallback in case vsync events do not arrive (e.g. around display
-    // off/on transitions); mirrors the v11/v20 vsync timeout strategy.
+    // Deliver on the next event-loop pass instead of from the vsync callback.
+    // set() already self-paces against the panel's TE (swap() no longer waits
+    // for vsync), so holding delivery to vsync only added up to one period of
+    // input latency. A static scene still stops requesting updates.
     if (!m_deliverUpdateTimeout.isActive())
-        m_deliverUpdateTimeout.start(50, this);
+        m_deliverUpdateTimeout.start(0, this);
 
     return true;
 }
